From c0780c242a83e7153d8fed4b7635e9bcb7860318 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy Fiddaman <illumos@fiddaman.net>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:08:05 +0000
Subject: testsuite: skip tests that conflict with -msave-args

-msave-args forces a frame pointer in every function, stores the
integer argument registers to the stack in the prologue, and disables
simple_return and therefore shrink-wrapping. The multilib test board
"-m64/-msave-args" therefore fails tests whose expectations are
about the exact prologue/epilogue, and so on.
